## Curated builds

Reviewed against patch 2.1.95 on 2026-08-18. The live patch is 2.2.16a, so these have not been re-read against it yet.

### Mid Lane Standard (Mid)

- Items: Arcane Boots, Clock of Destiny, Lightning Truncheon, Genius Wand, Divine Glaive, Blood Wings
- Core: Clock of Destiny, Lightning Truncheon, Divine Glaive
- Emblem: Mage Emblem with Rupture, Bargain Hunter, Impure Rage
- Battle spell: Flameshot
- Flex: Holy Crystal over Blood Wings when Use when your frontline is protecting you and the enemy backline is reachable through Astral Echo. Raw Magic Power is stronger than the shield in clean poke games.; Winter Crown over Blood Wings when Enemy has a committed backline diver such as Ling, Fanny, Hayabusa, Natalia, or Gusion. Frozen buys the one window Novaria needs to reset through a wall.; Glowing Wand over Genius Wand when Enemy sustain is keeping frontliners alive through poke. Lifebane matters more than early Magic Defense shred against healer or regen-heavy drafts.
- Total cost: 11040 gold

Default protected-mid setup. Clock of Destiny and Lightning Truncheon create the first real poke spike, then penetration keeps Star Shatter relevant once enemies buy magic defense.

### Frontline Control (Mid)

- Items: Magic Boots, Enchanted Talisman, Ice Queen Wand, Glowing Wand, Wishing Lantern, Divine Glaive
- Core: Enchanted Talisman, Ice Queen Wand, Glowing Wand
- Emblem: Mage Emblem with Agility, Bargain Hunter, Impure Rage
- Battle spell: Flameshot
- Flex: Clock of Destiny over Ice Queen Wand when Your team already has enough slows and needs you to scale harder into objective fights. Clock adds durability and mana without giving up the poke plan.; Genius Wand over Wishing Lantern when Enemy frontliners are buying magic defense earlier than health. Genius Wand softens targets before Divine Glaive becomes the main damage multiplier.; Blood Wings over Wishing Lantern when Enemy poke reaches you before fights start. Blood Wings turns repeated pre-fight chip into a shield trade instead of a forced recall.
- Total cost: 11090 gold

Use this into tanky or sustain-heavy drafts where Novaria's job is repeated scouting, slows, and HP pressure rather than a single burst pick.

### Roam Vision (Roam)

- Items: Rapid Boots, Enchanted Talisman, Ice Queen Wand, Glowing Wand, Divine Glaive, Winter Crown
- Core: Enchanted Talisman, Ice Queen Wand, Glowing Wand
- Emblem: Support Emblem with Agility, Pull Yourself Together, Focusing Mark
- Battle spell: Flicker
- Blessing: Encourage
- Flex: Magic Boots over Rapid Boots when Enemy keeps forcing combat before you can rotate. Magic Boots keeps scouting and Astral Echo uptime steadier than the extra 15 Movement Speed.; Blood Wings over Winter Crown when Enemy lacks hard backline dive but chips you with long-range magic or marksman poke. The shield has more uptime than Frozen in slow sieges.; Dire Hit over Encourage when Use when Novaria plays alone on the flank all game, so the aura reaches nobody and the Force movement speed is worth more than the ally stats.; Sky Piercer over Winter Crown when Only buy when your team is already snowballing and you are finishing revealed low-HP targets without dying. Drop it if stacks stay low or dives reach you.
- Total cost: 10790 gold

Roam Novaria is a vision and tempo pick, not a primary damage source. Encourage feeds the carries she scouts for, where the revamped Dire Hit would spend its Force on every Astral Meteor poke, and Support Emblem shortens Flicker and Winter Crown windows.

